<title>UK: Core ups bid for Scott's enlarged capital.</title>
<headline>Core ups bid for Scott's enlarged capital.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Core Laboratories of the U.S. said on Wednesday that it would offer 59 pence per share for buying out the enlarged issued share capital of British oil engineering services firm Scott Pickford Plc, even if its planned share swap with Austrialian geoservices firm Aerodata Holdings goes ahead.</p>
<p>Core's offer valued Scott's enlarged issued capital at 8.9 million stg, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
